  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Malaria and Child Health Programme 2011 - 2015</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To reduce child mortality by increasing availability of preventable malaria commodities, essential medicines and malaria treatment, and strengthen epidemic responseTo improve the survival of pregnant women and children under-5 years by providing key malaria prevention and treatment measures and strengthening the drug supply chain.   This will benefit 786,000 children and 180,000 pregnant women by reducing malaria prevalence. This will avert the deaths of 32,850 children under 5 by 2015 and contributes towards the achievement of Millennium Development Goals 4 and 5.</narrative>
  </description>
